# Input
```css
/* should generate diagnostics */
$condition: true;
@if $condition {
  .conditional {}
  .conditional {}
}

@mixin duplicates {
  .mixin-selector {}
  .mixin-selector {}
}
@include duplicates;

@for $index from 1 through 2 {
  .loop-selector {}
  .loop-selector {}
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
scss-control-flow.invalid.scss:4:3 lint/suspicious/noDuplicateSelectors ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The selector list ".conditional" is defined more than once.
  
    2 │ $condition: true;
    3 │ @if $condition {
  > 4 │   .conditional {}
      │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    5 │   .conditional {}
    6 │ }
  
  i This rule repeats the same selector list.
  
    3 │ @if $condition {
    4 │   .conditional {}
  > 5 │   .conditional {}
      │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    6 │ }
    7 │ 
  
  i Declarations in the later rules can silently override the earlier ones, and duplicated rules make the stylesheet harder to maintain.
  
  i Remove or merge the duplicate rules to keep the stylesheet clean.
  

```

